From: NeuroCore OS Contributors <kernel@neurocore-os.org>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fbdev: fb_logo: default to single centered CLUT224 boot logo

Enables Linux 6.18's native single centered framebuffer boot logo defaults
(`fb_center_logo = true`, `fb_logo_count = 1`) in `drivers/video/fbdev/core/fb_logo.c`
instead of tiling one copy per CPU core across the top edge, while preserving
kernel command-line overrides (`fbcon=logo-count:...`).

Signed-off-by: NeuroCore OS Contributors <kernel@neurocore-os.org>
---
 drivers/video/fbdev/core/fb_logo.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fb_logo.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fb_logo.c
index 5550795f2a10..9c2e83c0f8d1 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fb_logo.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fb_logo.c
@@ -5,8 +5,8 @@
 
 #include "fb_internal.h"
 
-bool fb_center_logo __read_mostly;
-int fb_logo_count __read_mostly = -1;
+bool fb_center_logo __read_mostly = true;
+int fb_logo_count __read_mostly = 1;
 
 static inline unsigned int safe_shift(unsigned int d, int n)
 {
